# Arguments for the in-car drive service. One line, deliberately: the unit expands
# it unquoted so it splits on whitespace, and keeping the whole argument list here
# means switching a drive's mode is editing one file, not the unit.
#
# Installed to /etc/default/dsrc-drive. Not read from the repository at run time.
#
# --duration-s 0        no wall-clock limit; the drive ends when the phone stops
# --rebind-timeout-s 0  never give up on a phone that went away. The default of 120
#                       ends the run if the handset is absent longer than that, and
#                       in a car nothing is there to start it again.
# --phone-wait-s 600    ten minutes from service start to the first tap on the
#                       phone, which is the walk from the boot to the driver's seat.
# --headless            there is no display in the car.
#
# Shadow mode is the default. For a live-gating drive (task 51), add --live-rates.
# Quoted deliberately. systemd's EnvironmentFile takes the whole line after the
# "=" and needs no quotes, but the file then does NOT parse as shell -- sourcing
# it gives "--usb: command not found", because an unquoted value with spaces
# reads as a command with a one-variable environment. Quoting satisfies both
# parsers: systemd strips the quotes, and `. dsrc-drive.env` works for anyone
# checking what the service will run.
DSRC_RUN_ARGS="--phone --usb --headless --duration-s 0 --rebind-timeout-s 0 --phone-wait-s 600 --print-every 30"
